# Kung Pao Chicken

Based on [The Woks of Life](https://thewoksoflife.com/kung-pao-chicken/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Peanuts

- [ ] 1 tsp [vegetable oil, for peanuts]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-peanuts" }
- [ ] 1 cup [raw shelled peanuts]{ ing="raw-shelled-peanuts" } (with or without the skin)

### Chicken and Marinade

- [ ] 12 oz [chicken breast]{ ing="chicken-breast" }, cut into 3/4-inch cubes (or boneless skinless chicken thighs)
- [ ] 1 tsp [vegetable oil, for the marinade]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-the-marinade" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cornstarch, for the marinade]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-marinade" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [Shaoxing wine]{ ing="shaoxing-wine" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 pinch [white pepper]{ ing="white-pepper" }

### Sauce

- [ ] 1 Tbsp [light soy sauce]{ ing="light-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [rice wine vinegar]{ ing="rice-wine-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] 3 Tbsps [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [cornstarch, for the sauce]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-sauce" }

### Stir-Fry

- [ ] 3 Tbsps [oil]{ ing="oil" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, smashed and sliced
- [ ] 2 thin slices [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, minced
- [ ] 2 [dried red chilies]{ ing="dried-red-chilies" }, deseeded and chopped
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Sichuan peppercorn powder]{ ing="sichuan-peppercorn-powder" }
- [ ] 6 [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }, white portions only, cut into 3/4-inch pieces

## Recipe

1. Heat 1 tsp [oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-peanuts" } in a wok or pan over medium heat and add 1 cup [raw shelled peanuts]{ ing="raw-shelled-peanuts" }. Stir constantly (or they’ll burn) for 3 minutes. Turn off the heat and stir for another minute using the residual heat in the wok. Set aside to cool completely so they turn crunchy.
1. Combine the [chicken]{ ing="chicken-breast" } with 1 tsp each of [oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil-for-the-marinade" }, [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-marinade" }, and [Shaoxing wine]{ ing="shaoxing-wine" }, 1/8 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and a pinch of [white pepper]{ ing="white-pepper" }. Set aside to marinate for 20 minutes.
1. In a small bowl, mix together [light soy sauce]{ ing="light-soy-sauce" }, [dark soy sauce]{ ing="dark-soy-sauce" }, [rice wine vinegar]{ ing="rice-wine-vinegar" }, [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }, [water]{ ing="water" }, and [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch-for-the-sauce" }. Set aside.
1. Heat 2 Tbsps [oil]{ ing="oil" } in a wok or large skillet over high heat. Sear the chicken, remove from the wok to a bowl, and set aside.
1. Turn the heat to low and add another Tbsp oil. Add the [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [ginger]{ ing="ginger" }, [chilies]{ ing="dried-red-chilies" }, [Sichuan peppercorn powder]{ ing="sichuan-peppercorn-powder" }, and [scallions]{ ing="scallions" }. Cook for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.
1. Add the chicken back to the pan and turn the heat to high. Stir-fry for 1 minute, then stir up the prepared sauce so the settled cornstarch is incorporated. Add the sauce to the wok and stir-fry for another minute; the sauce should thicken very quickly.
1. Add the peanuts, give everything a final stir, and serve.

## Notes

- Substitute roasted shelled peanuts and skip the first step.
- Boneless skinless chicken thighs can replace the chicken breast.
- Dried red chilies can be quite spicy; adjust to taste.
